{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Behold, I stand before you there, upon the rock at Horeb.</b> This rock in Rephidim is the rock at Kadesh — they are all one, and it was the well of Miriam, and it traveled with them all the days of the wilderness. This is why it says הנני, in the same language spoken concerning the manna — הנני ממטיר לכם — to teach that just as the manna sustained Israel forty years, so did this well sustain them. And furthermore, just as the Shekhinah was revealed in the manna, as it says, וראיתם את כבוד ה׳, so was it revealed here upon the rock for the well, for the matter of the well was an enduring wonder like the wonder of the manna." "<b>And you shall strike the rock.</b> They said in the Midrash: from here we learn that the staff was of sapphire, for it says והכית בצור — 'you shall strike בצור' — it does not say על הצור, 'upon the rock,' but בצור, 'in the rock.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:00:24.238377898Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}